#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:2
msgid "Issue Management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:4
msgid ""
"Bugs, feature requests and other things we need to do are tracked as Github "
"issues. Issues can be of various types and in various states, and also "
"belong to milestones or not. This page is an attempt to document the current "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:10
msgid "Labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:12
msgid ""
"Issues without labels are undecided - that is, we don't yet know if it's a "
"bug, a configuration issue, a feature request or what. Issues that are "
"invalid for whatever reason are closed with a short explanation of why. "
"Examples include \"Duplicate of #123\", \"Discovered to be configuration "
"error\", \"Rendered moot by #123\" and so on. We don't use the \"invalid\" "
"or \"wontfix\" labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:19
msgid "android"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:20
msgid "Marks an issue as occurring on the Android platform only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:22
msgid "bug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:23
msgid "The issue is a verified bug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:25
msgid "build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:26
msgid ""
"The issue is caused by or requires changes to the build system (scripts or "
"Docker image)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:29
msgid "docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:30
msgid "Something requires documenting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:32
msgid "easy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:33
msgid ""
"This could be easily fixed, probably an hour's work or less. These issues "
"are good starting points for new contributors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:36
msgid "enhancement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:37
msgid ""
"This is a new feature or an improvement of some kind, as opposed to a "
"problem (bug)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:40
msgid "help-wanted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:41
msgid ""
"The core team can't or won't do this, but someone else is welcome to. This "
"does not mean that help is not wanted on the *other* issues. You can see "
"this as a soft ``wontfix``. (A hard ``wontfix`` is simply a close with a "
"short explanation why.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:46
msgid "pr-bugfix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:47
msgid ""
"This pull request *fixes* a bug. This is different from the ``bug`` label, "
"as there may also be pull requests with for example tests that *prove* a bug "
"which would then be labeled ``bug``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:51
msgid "pr-refactor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:52
msgid ""
"This pull request is a refactoring, i.e. not supposed to change behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:55
msgid "pr-WIP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:56
msgid ""
"This pull request is not ready for merging, even if the tests pass and it "
"looks good. It is incomplete or requires more discussion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:60
msgid "protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:61
msgid "This requires a change to the protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:64
msgid "Milestone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:66
msgid ""
"There are milestones for major and sometimes minor versions. An issue being "
"assigned to a milestone means it is a blocker - the release can't be made "
"without the issue being closed. Issues not assigned to a milestone can be "
"handled whenever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:72
msgid "Assignee"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:74
msgid ""
"Users can be assigned to issues. We don't usually do so. Sometimes someone "
"assigns themself to an issue to indicate \"I'm working on this\" to avoid "
"others doing so too. It's not mandatory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:79
msgid "Locking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:81
msgid ""
"We don't normally lock issues (prevent further discussion on them). There "
"are some exceptions though;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:84
msgid ""
"\"Popular\" issues that attract lots of \"me too\" and \"+1\" comments. "
"These are noise and annoy people with useless notifications via mail and in "
"the Github interface. Once the issue is clear and it suffers from this "
"symptom I may lock it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:89
msgid ""
"Contentious bikeshedding discussions. After two sides in a discussion have "
"clarified their points, there is no point arguing endlessly about it. As "
"above, this may get closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/issues.rst:93
msgid ""
"Duplicates. Once an issue has been identified as a duplicate of another "
"issue, it may be locked to prevent further discussion there. The intention "
"is to move the discussion to the other (referenced) issue, while someone "
"just doing a search and jumping on the first match might otherwise resurrect "
"discussion in the duplicate."
msgstr ""
